00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:36.890
So it all starts
with this global VPC.

00:07:36.890 --> 00:07:39.860
The idea of a global
VPC is that we

00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:43.850
can have multiple clients
running on the same network,

00:07:43.850 --> 00:07:47.210
using overlapping
network name spaces.

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:50.210
We all use 10.0 for something.

00:07:50.210 --> 00:07:55.580
But they're all sharing the
same network infrastructure.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:07:57.950
So this requires us to build
functional and performance

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:01.115
isolation for all for
all of our clients.

00:08:05.573 --> 00:08:07.832
Oops.

